<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Lint configuration for this module.

    Everything suppressed here is a deliberate product decision, not an oversight, and each
    entry carries the reason. Anything actionable is fixed in the code instead of being
    silenced, so a warning that appears in a build log is worth reading.
-->
<lint>

    <!--
        ===================================================================
        Icon shape
        ===================================================================

        The launcher bitmaps are the square Immich flower artwork, generated from
        immich-provider.png. They intentionally fill the canvas and are paired with the
        adaptive icon in mipmap-anydpi-v26, which supplies the mask on API 26+, the only
        API levels this app runs on. The legacy PNG therefore never renders unmasked in
        practice, so padding it would only shrink the artwork where it *is* used.
    -->
    <issue id="IconLauncherShape" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
        `roundIcon` was removed from the manifest: it pointed at the same square bitmap as
        `icon`, which is what IconLauncherShape flagged, and the adaptive icon already
        provides the circular treatment.

        The `mipmap-anydpi-v26` folder stays even though minSdk is 26, so the qualifier is
        redundant (ObsoleteSdkInt). Moving it to `mipmap-anydpi` makes the adaptive XML
        collide with the per-density legacy `ic_launcher.png` files, which is a worse
        problem than a redundant qualifier. Ignored here rather than by an inline
        tools:ignore, because a directory has no root element to annotate.
    -->
    <issue id="ObsoleteSdkInt">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26" />
    </issue>

    <!--
        ===================================================================
        Network security
        ===================================================================

        Cleartext HTTP and user-installed CAs are required, not accidental:

          - A LAN Immich at http://192.168.x.x:2283 is the default self-hosted setup.
          - The "Custom CA (PEM)" setting exists precisely so a user-supplied CA can be
            trusted. Refusing user anchors would make that feature impossible.

        Both are documented in README.md under "Security notes". See also the inline
        justification in res/xml/network_security_config.xml.
    -->
    <issue id="InsecureBaseConfiguration" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="AcceptsUserCertificates" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
        TlsTrust installs a custom X509TrustManager for the two opt-in modes (accept any
        certificate / trust one PEM). It is the only way to express "trust exactly this
        CA" through OkHttp without writing the trust store to disk. It is not used for the
        default configuration, which goes through the platform trust manager.
    -->
    <issue id="CustomX509TrustManager" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
        ===================================================================
        Dependency freshness
        ===================================================================

        Both checks compare against whatever is newest on the network at build time, which
        makes them fail on a schedule unrelated to this project and would otherwise turn a
        green build red with no code change.

        Versions are pinned deliberately in app/build.gradle.kts, each with a comment
        explaining the ceiling (for example: Compose BOM 2026.06.01 is the newest that does
        not require compileSdk 37, and okhttp 5.5+ wants compileSdk 37 as well). Updating
        them is a planned task with a compileSdk bump, not a side effect of running lint.
    -->
    <issue id="GradleDependency" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="NewerVersionAvailable" severity="ignore" />
    <issue id="AndroidGradlePluginVersion" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
        ===================================================================
        Intent forwarding in the picker bridge
        ===================================================================

        SafPickerBridgeActivity is exported on purpose: the system photo picker only lists
        apps that answer the intent, so being callable is the entire point. It therefore
        receives an intent from an untrusted caller, which is what the check is warning
        about.

        The forwarded intent is not the caller's. It is built from scratch with
        ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT, and only three values are carried over (the MIME type, the
        MIME type list and EXTRA_ALLOW_MULTIPLE), each re-validated against an allowlist in
        sanitizeType/sanitizeTypes. No component, data URI, action, flag or other extra is
        reused, so there is no confused-deputy path to sanitise.

        Lint cannot verify this because the taint propagates through getStringArrayExtra,
        so the finding is acknowledged here rather than silenced at the call site.
    -->
    <issue id="UnsafeIntentLaunch">
        <ignore path="src/main/kotlin/dev/immich/picker/ui/SafPickerBridgeActivity.kt" />
    </issue>

</lint>
